[2026-01-30T13:45:25.132Z] [STDOUT] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UVYUyd8AYe6ABSUn9thJDr","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n     2→\n     3→## REQUIREMENT\n     4→\n     5→# Unify confidence filtering logic across tabs\n     6→\n     7→## Metadata\n     8→- **Category**: maintenance\n     9→- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    10→- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n    11→- **Scan Type**: pragmatic_integrator\n    12→- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:29:35 AM\n    13→\n    14→## Description\n    15→FindingsTab and SourcesTab both implement identical confidence filtering logic with the same thresholds (high>=0.8, medium 0.5-0.8, low<0.5). Extract to a shared filterByConfidence utility function that both tabs import to eliminate code duplication.\n    16→\n    17→## Reasoning\n    18→Same filtering logic copied in two places means bugs could be introduced inconsistently. A shared utility ensures the thresholds stay in sync and reduces cognitive load when maintaining filter behavior.\n    19→\n    20→## Context\n    21→\n    22→**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n    23→\n    24→### Context: Report Tabs\n    25→\n    26→**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n    27→**Related Files**:\n    28→- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n    29→- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n    30→- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n    31→- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n    32→- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n    33→- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n    34→- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n    35→\n    36→**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n    37→\n    38→## Recommended Skills\n    39→\n    40→Use Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n    41→\n    42→## Notes\n    43→\n    44→This requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n    45→\n    46→## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n    47→\n    48→1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n    49→   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n    50→   - title: 2-6 word summary\n    51→   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n    52→\n    53→2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n    54→   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n    55→   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n    56→\n    57→3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n    58→\n    59→Begin implementation now.\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"bbdddf83-efc9-404e-b6a3-e0a9e67b2ab3","uuid":"3e6008e3-f756-4f76-9610-59864cc74f7e","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"C:\\Users\\mkdol\\dolla\\res\\.claude\\commands\\idea-6d3dbb3e-unify-confidence-filtering-log.md","content":"Execute this requirement immediately without asking questions.\n\n## REQUIREMENT\n\n# Unify confidence filtering logic across tabs\n\n## Metadata\n- **Category**: maintenance\n- **Effort**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Impact**: Unknown (N/A/3)\n- **Scan Type**: pragmatic_integrator\n- **Generated**: 1/30/2026, 1:29:35 AM\n\n## Description\nFindingsTab and SourcesTab both implement identical confidence filtering logic with the same thresholds (high>=0.8, medium 0.5-0.8, low<0.5). Extract to a shared filterByConfidence utility function that both tabs import to eliminate code duplication.\n\n## Reasoning\nSame filtering logic copied in two places means bugs could be introduced inconsistently. A shared utility ensures the thresholds stay in sync and reduces cognitive load when maintaining filter behavior.\n\n## Context\n\n**Note**: This section provides supporting architectural documentation and is NOT a hard requirement. Use it as guidance to understand existing code structure and maintain consistency.\n\n### Context: Report Tabs\n\n**Description**: Tab-based navigation components for quick-access report sections. Provides compact, scannable summaries for overview, findings, sources, entities, analysis, and perspectives.\n**Related Files**:\n- `src/components/report/tabs/OverviewTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/FindingsTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/SourcesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/EntitiesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/AnalysisTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/PerspectivesTab.tsx`\n- `src/components/report/tabs/index.tsx`\n\n**Post-Implementation**: After completing this requirement, evaluate if the context description or file paths need updates. Use the appropriate API/DB query to update the context if architectural changes were made.\n\n## Recommended Skills\n\nUse Claude Code skills as appropriate for implementation guidance. Check `.claude/skills/` directory for available skills.\n\n## Notes\n\nThis requirement was generated from an AI-evaluated project idea. No specific goal is associated with this idea.\n\n## AFTER IMPLEMENTATION\n\n1. Log your implementation using the `log_implementation` MCP tool with:\n   - requirementName: the requirement filename (without .md)\n   - title: 2-6 word summary\n   - overview: 1-2 paragraphs describing what was done\n\n2. Check for test scenario using `check_test_scenario` MCP tool\n   - If hasScenario is true, call `capture_screenshot` tool\n   - If hasScenario is false, skip screenshot\n\n3. Verify: `npx tsc --noEmit` (fix any type errors)\n\nBegin implementation now.","numLines":59,"startLine":1,"totalLines":59}}}
